{"id": "Q085", "card": {"answer_id": "550", "kb_version": 49, "as_of": null, "superseded_since": null, "client": "Arvana Group", "route": "calculator:ap.price", "status": "answered", "rule": {"text": "No — the line cannot pass the price match: the excess of ₹400 on the line is above the applicable limit of ₹395, so the line is held with exception PRICE_VAR. [1] The rule is that where the invoice unit price is higher than the PO unit price, the line passes only if the total excess on that line is no more than the lower of 1% of the PO line value and ₹500. [1] Here 1% of the PO line value is ₹395 and the cap is ₹500, so the limit is ₹395, and the ₹400 excess is not within it. [1] A line that fails is held with exception PRICE_VAR and sent to the buyer who raised the PO, who either amends the PO or asks the supplier for a credit note. [1] In practice, the note to the buyer should state the line, the invoice and PO unit prices, the excess amount and that it is above the limit, and ask for the PO to be amended or a credit note obtained. [2]", "citations": [{"n": 1, "passage_id": "6a3d60030fef8254dc43", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v4.0_2026.docx", "short_label": "AP SOP v4.0 §4.2", "locator": "4.2", "section_title": "Price tolerance", "doc_type": "sop", "status": "current", "quote": "the line passes only if the total excess on that line is no more than the lower of 1% of the PO line value and ₹500"}, {"n": 2, "passage_id": "a1c5bb42d73893644924", "file": "PS-07_training_and_expert_transcripts.docx", "short_label": "Video 3 [03:10]", "locator": "Video 3 [03:10]", "section_title": "Working the exception queue", "doc_type": "training", "status": "current", "quote": "Please amend PO or get a credit note.'"}]}, "working": [{"label": "PO line value (₹395 × 100)", "value": "₹39,500"}, {"label": "Excess on line (₹4 × 100)", "value": "₹400"}, {"label": "1% of PO line value", "value": "₹395"}, {"label": "Cap", "value": "₹500"}, {"label": "Limit (lower of the two)", "value": "₹395"}, {"la